I believe something's gonna happen

14:03.443 --> 14:05.778
that will put me
out of contention for a rose.

14:07.180 --> 14:08.614
And that thing just happened.

14:08.615 --> 14:09.915
Farewell, and thank you

14:09.916 --> 14:12.117
for feeding me champagne
and shrimp all day.

14:16.890 --> 14:18.524
Reporting live from Quahog Prison,

14:18.525 --> 14:20.559
I'm Joe Horrigan, Channel Five News.

14:20.560 --> 14:22.861
Thanks, Joe.
Great reporting, terrible eyes.

14:22.862 --> 14:24.663
Switching gears now, I'd like to talk

14:24.664 --> 14:26.732
about the crime situation
here in Quahog.

14:26.733 --> 14:29.868
Joining me now is white-haired
contributor Peter Griffin.

14:29.869 --> 14:32.638
Peter, what are you hearing
about crime in Quahog?

14:32.639 --> 14:35.407
Uh... you know, not much.

14:35.408 --> 14:38.010
Not much? Excuse us for one moment.

14:39.531 --> 14:40.946
- What are you doing?!
- What?

14:40.947 --> 14:42.414
I don't know anything about crime.

14:42.415 --> 14:45.084
So? People want to know that
bad stuff's going on out there.

14:45.085 --> 14:46.485
That's why they watch the news.

14:46.486 --> 14:48.654
- You want me to make stuff up?
- I don't know.

14:48.655 --> 14:50.623
I thought you had white hair.

14:50.624 --> 14:53.826
- You're right, I do.
- Of course you do.

14:56.396 --> 14:58.397
Now, you were talking about crime?

14:58.398 --> 15:00.399
Crime is way up, and you know why?

15:00.400 --> 15:01.834
'Cause of immigrants.

15:01.835 --> 15:03.302
I say, as Americans,

15:03.303 --> 15:05.738
we should all take a pledge
to kick 'em out.

15:05.739 --> 15:09.141
Only pledge I stand for is Lemon Pledge.

15:15.682 --> 15:18.817
Peter Griffin, white hair, very
credible, thank you so much.

15:18.818 --> 15:21.453
Coming up, lost dog comes home...

15:21.454 --> 15:23.689
one piece at a time.

15:28.094 --> 15:29.928
Peter, that was amazing.

15:29.929 --> 15:31.830
I'm the news director
here at Channel Five.

15:31.831 --> 15:34.400
How would you like to do
what you just did every night?

15:34.401 --> 15:35.968
Wipe a bloody booger under the desk?

15:35.969 --> 15:37.970
No, I'm asking you to join us full-time

15:37.971 --> 15:40.039
to be our permanent senior analyst.

15:40.040 --> 15:42.374
Would you excuse me
while I step into another room

15:42.375 --> 15:45.644
and celebrate like a girl in a
Rom-com who just got good news?

15:48.281 --> 15:50.401
Aah! The Sanguelto!

15:50.402 --> 15:52.785
My blood's thinner than water!

15:54.354 --> 15:56.355
<i>If taking Sanguelto,</i>

15:56.356 --> 15:58.624
<i>please refrain
from dancing like in a Rom-com,</i>

15:58.625 --> 16:00.693
<i>as nosebleeds may be permanent.</i>

16:00.694 --> 16:03.429
<i>And remember, most drugs
are prescribed to you</i>

16:03.430 --> 16:05.597
<i>because a hot girl
with a rolling suitcase</i>

16:05.598 --> 16:07.599
<i>gave your doctor a free pen.</i>

16:15.414 --> 16:17.582
Peter, what the hell
do you think you're doing?

16:17.583 --> 16:20.585
Who says you can just make
things up and call them facts?

16:20.586 --> 16:22.420
Tom Tucker did. He kissed me.

16:22.421 --> 16:24.956
You have a responsibility
as a member of the press

16:24.957 --> 16:27.158
to report the news accurately.

16:27.159 --> 16:30.595
You can't just say crazy things
that aren't in any way true.

16:30.596 --> 16:34.131
Yeah, leave that to the yahoos in D.C.

16:35.334 --> 16:37.912
- Did that get a "That's So Joe"?
- No!

16:37.913 --> 16:39.677
Okay, well, what are the rules on that?

16:39.678 --> 16:41.145
We're still working that out.

16:41.146 --> 16:43.207
Well, let me know
when you decide on the rules.

16:43.208 --> 16:46.010
I'm really excited
about working on this.

16:46.011 --> 16:48.079
With you guys.

16:52.117 --> 16:54.752
Chris, welcome
to the lingerie department.

16:54.753 --> 16:56.287
What are we doing here?

16:56.288 --> 16:58.789
When I was young, seeing
these half-naked mannequins

16:58.790 --> 17:00.625
was all I needed to get me going.

17:00.626 --> 17:02.093
What's the endgame here...

17:02.094 --> 17:03.961
Him walking around Macy's with a chub?

17:03.962 --> 17:06.163
No, we've got
to reset his arousal meter.

17:06.164 --> 17:08.633
He needs to be able
to use his imagination again.

17:08.634 --> 17:10.835
Any of these mannequins
doing anything for you, Chris?

17:10.836 --> 17:12.837
Uh, I don't know.

17:12.838 --> 17:15.406
I guess the one
without a head is pretty cool.

17:15.407 --> 17:17.642
All right, that's... that's something.

17:17.643 --> 17:20.912
And that bin of chopped-up ones
over there... that could be okay.

17:20.913 --> 17:24.015
'Specially the one
that looks kind of afraid.

17:24.016 --> 17:26.017
There you go. Look at you.

17:26.018 --> 17:28.185
Sounds like someone is ready
for that date.

17:28.186 --> 17:29.687
Do you gentlemen need any help?

17:29.688 --> 17:30.922
No, thank you, dear.

17:30.923 --> 17:33.591
We're just trying
to get my brother to full mast.

17:36.628 --> 17:39.563
We want to welcome back our new
permanent senior analyst,

17:39.564 --> 17:41.532
Peter Griffin and his white hair.

17:41.533 --> 17:43.367
What's the latest on crime in Quahog?

17:43.368 --> 17:45.836
- Tom, crime is up.
- Wow. How high?

17:45.837 --> 17:48.450
- All the way to the top.
- Whoa. The top.

17:48.451 --> 17:50.841
Has it ever been all the way
to the top before, Peter?

17:50.842 --> 17:53.044
Never. In fact, we had to raise the top.

17:53.045 --> 17:55.713
So, the new top is even higher
than the old top?

17:55.714 --> 17:57.615
Yes, the old top is now the middle.

17:57.616 --> 17:59.183
<i>And The Middle is a show</i>

17:59.184 --> 18:01.886
that was inexplicably on ABC
for a very long time.

18:01.887 --> 18:03.354
How many seasons?

18:03.355 --> 18:05.556
It might be, like, 11.
I'm not even kidding.

18:05.557 --> 18:08.292
Peter Griffin, white hair, very
credible, thank you so much.

18:08.293 --> 18:10.394
Coming up, we'll tell you where to look

18:10.395 --> 18:13.397
when a person has a birthmark
on their face.

18:17.102 --> 18:19.971
So, Chris, have you weaned
yourself off of Internet porn?

18:19.972 --> 18:23.174
Wait. I thought the whole point
was to not wean myself off.

18:23.175 --> 18:26.043
No, Chris, I mean,
have you stopped...? Never mind.

18:26.044 --> 18:28.379
- You ready for your date?
- You bet I am!

18:32.568 --> 18:34.136
Hi, Chris.

18:35.304 --> 18:37.005
Hi, Kristen.

18:37.006 --> 18:39.474
Ready to see a Marvel movie,
'cause I chose?

18:39.475 --> 18:41.810
Sure. And for sure this is a real date,

18:41.811 --> 18:43.278
and me and the popular kids

18:43.279 --> 18:45.947
aren't gonna thrill-kill you tonight.

18:45.948 --> 18:48.750
I think Chris is gonna be just fine.

18:51.754 --> 18:54.423
Which is more than I can say
for our pizza.

18:57.093 --> 18:58.593
Oh, man.

19:06.803 --> 19:09.171
Well, I hope you're happy.

19:09.172 --> 19:12.441
You're telling lies on the news
just to boost your own ego.

19:12.442 --> 19:14.142
It's pronounced "Eggo," Lois,

19:14.143 --> 19:16.344
and I will thank you to leggo of mine.

19:16.345 --> 19:18.146
Peter, fake news is a real problem

19:18.147 --> 19:19.848
in this country right now,

19:19.849 --> 19:22.984
and I really don't want
my husband contributing to it.

19:22.985 --> 19:24.853
Maybe you're right.

19:24.854 --> 19:27.155
It doesn't feel good lying all the time.

19:27.156 --> 19:28.857
I guess I just like all the attention

19:28.858 --> 19:30.459
that came along with having white hair.

19:30.460 --> 19:33.128
Well, I don't think that's
the kind of attention you want.

19:33.129 --> 19:35.197
And it's certainly not
the kind of attention

19:35.198 --> 19:36.865
I want for our family.

19:36.866 --> 19:39.501
You know what?
If it means that much to you,

19:39.502 --> 19:41.803
I'll tell Tom
that I won't do it anymore.

19:41.804 --> 19:43.672
- Really?
- Really.

19:43.673 --> 19:46.208
Oh, Peter, that makes me so happy.

19:48.711 --> 19:50.712
Hello? Donald Trump?!

19:50.713 --> 19:52.380
You saw me on the news?

19:52.381 --> 19:55.383
You want me to be your press
secretary in the next episode?

19:55.384 --> 19:57.018
Why, sure, I'd love to!

19:57.019 --> 19:59.187
We'll get started drawing it right away.

19:59.188 --> 20:00.655
Lois, pack your bags.

20:00.656 --> 20:03.758
We're joining the Trump Administration.

20:09.565 --> 20:12.067
Just what Washington needs, huh?

20:12.068 --> 20:14.002
Another talking head.

20:15.805 --> 20:18.240
Oh, man.

20:21.395 --> 20:23.396
<i>Next week on Family Guy...</i>

20:23.397 --> 20:25.966
Hey, Dad, I want you
to meet my new friend, Meg.

20:25.967 --> 20:29.469
Pleased to meet you, Meg.
You have a beautiful rack.

20:29.470 --> 20:30.670
Oh, thanks.

20:30.671 --> 20:32.973
I was talking to my daughter.

20:40.314 --> 20:43.316
And now, please welcome
Mr. Bruce Jenner.

21:00.495 --> 21:03.264
Just wanted to remind you fellas
what you're all fighting for.

21:03.906 --> 21:07.412
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv